Title: M16 final checks
Author: Math++ validation run

Run on branch `fix/validation` (the complete product), Windows 11, release build, 2026-11-20. Each check lists the command, the result and the fixes made.

## 1. Release build

Command: `cargo build --release` (whole workspace).

Result: pass. Builds `mpp.exe` and `Math++.exe` with no warnings.

## 2. Tests

Command: `cargo test --workspace`.

Result: pass. 1431 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored, in 106 test binaries.

The count covers unit tests, property tests, the golden-example tests (`crates/mpp-cli/tests/examples.rs`, one per example, now including `long-worksheet`), the export snapshots, and the egui_kittest UI snapshot tests.

Fix: the new `long-worksheet` example needed export snapshots (`crates/mpp-export/tests/snapshots/long-worksheet.html` and `.tex`) and an expected-output file; both are added.

## 3. Lint, format, no Markdown

Commands: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all --check`, `git ls-files '*.md'`.

Result: pass. Clippy has no warnings, fmt reports nothing to change, and no tracked Markdown file exists.

## 4. Licences

Command: `cargo deny check licenses` (cargo-deny 0.22.0, installed for this run).

Result: pass, with one item for Ben. A `deny.toml` is added that allows MIT, Apache-2.0 (also with the LLVM exception), BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, Unicode-DFS-2016, OFL-1.1, CC0-1.0 and BSL-1.0. MPL-2.0 is not needed by any dependency, so it is not allowed.

Needs Ben: one crate, `epaint_default_fonts` (egui's bundled editor fonts: Hack, Ubuntu-Light and an emoji icon font), is licensed `(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND OFL-1.1 AND Ubuntu-font-1.0`. The Ubuntu Font Licence is free but not on the permissive list, so it is not allowed globally. It is excepted for that one crate only, with a comment in `deny.toml`. Decide whether to keep the exception or drop egui's default fonts (the page itself uses Latin Modern).

Fonts: the licences ship. `work/release/licences/` holds the GUST Latin Modern licence, the OFL text for egui's fonts, the Hack licence, the Ubuntu Font Licence and the emoji font's MIT licence, and `install-test.ps1` checks the first two are installed beside the program.

## 5. Live-edit speed

Command: `cargo test --release -p mpp-ide --test m16 -- --nocapture` (test `a_live_edit_in_the_long_worksheet_is_fast`).

Example: `examples/long-worksheet.mpp`, 299 lines: 16 sections of prose, definitions, derivatives, integrals and limits, then a figure.

Result: pass, far under the limit. One character typed in the middle, worst of 5 runs:

- Evaluator, `Session::update`: 3.7 ms (limit 100 ms).
- IDE, edit, re-evaluate, re-layout and paint of the page: 17.9 ms (limit 100 ms).

The test asserts both limits in release builds, so a slowdown fails the suite. No fix needed.

## 6. IDE screenshots

Command: `cargo test --release -p mpp-ide --test m16` (tests `every_example_has_a_screenshot_and_no_raw_source` and `each_problem_kind_is_shown_in_place`). Light theme, 1180 by 1500 pixels, saved to `target/m16-screens/`.

Result: pass after two fixes. Every example (31, with `imports` taken from its `main.mpp`) is drawn and checked for raw source such as `$$`, `\frac` and `\int`. Looked at: integrals, matrices, units, proofs, paper-features, graphs-3d, visual-calculus, long-worksheet, plus several problem screenshots.

Problem kinds in place (`error-*.png`): empty box, undefined name (with a "did you mean" hint), missing bracket, unit mismatch, numeric-fallback warning, assumption warning, import error (a file with errors and a missing file).

Fixes:

- Import line, missing file: the note "Can't find missing-file.mpp." was drawn over the words "Imports missing-file". The problem box covered only a few pixels of the line; it now covers the whole import line (`crates/mpp-ide/src/diagnostics/mod.rs`). Test: the box must be wider than 120 px.
- Figure labels: the legend said "tangentline" and the readouts under graphs said "tangentatx = 1:y = x - 2" (spaces lost, words in italics). Legend labels with spaces are now text (`crates/mpp-plot/src/spec.rs`), and readouts keep their words and spacing (`crates/mpp-ide/src/figure.rs`). Test: `figure_readouts_and_legend_labels_keep_their_spaces`.

## 7. Pipeline tests

Command: `cargo test -p mpp-cli --test pipeline -- --nocapture`.

Result: 16 of 23 documents pass; the 3 harness tests pass. No document or expectation was edited. All 12 proof documents are within their expectations except `navier-stokes.mpp` (below); nothing is reported as more proved than expected. The 7 failures are all missing features or decisions, so they are for Ben:

- `navier-stokes.mpp`: the proof statuses are right. The failing line is the Lean export check: Lemmas 3, 4 and 5 are checked numerically on a field instance, and vector calculus on fields has no Lean translation, so those steps export as `sorry`, while the expectation says "no sorry on its checked steps". Needs a Lean translation for field calculus, or a changed expectation.
- `labs/01-projectile-drag.mpp` and `labs/02-pendulum.mpp`: `T \approx ?` asks for a time measured from a solved ODE (the first maximum or landing time) and no such measure exists; `T` has no value.
- `labs/03-damped-spring.mpp`: the result 0.9954517249 is correct but the check wants it written as 0.9954 (a rounding rule for the check, or a precision written in the document).
- `labs/06-reaction-kinetics.mpp`: 6 parse errors (a concentration written `[A](t)` is not a function head), so the rate ratio, `[A](60)` and the fitted activation energy have no value.
- `labs/07-boyles-law.mpp`: `R^2` is read as the gas constant `R` squared, because the lab defines `R`. The regression `R^2` and a user's `R` collide; needs a decision on naming.
- `labs/11-monte-carlo-pi.mpp`: `p` has no value, so `sigma` cannot be worked out (the document relies on a measured fraction that is not defined as a value).

## 8. Exports

Commands: `mpp export <example> --to pdf|tex|html -o target/m16-export/...` for all 31 examples (93 files), then the PDFs were parsed and rasterised with pdfium (pypdfium2, installed into `target/scratch` only).

Result: pass after one fix. Every export succeeded (0 failures); all 31 PDFs parse (1 to 12 pages each). First pages of paper-features, proofs, integrals and graphs-3d were rasterised and looked at; the layout, typeset maths, results in blue, theorem blocks, references and figures are right.

Fix: in `proofs.pdf` each proof that ended in a numbered list showed a second, lonely end mark on its own line, because the written end mark on the line after the last step was added to again. The export now shows one (`crates/mpp-export/src/pdf/compose.rs`, test `a_proof_ending_in_a_list_shows_one_end_mark`).

Observation, no change: a figure that does not fit under the text moves to the next page (graphs-3d has about half a page of white after the first surface). Taste call.

## 9. Installer

Commands: `pwsh work/release/build.ps1`, then `pwsh work/release/install-test.ps1`.

Result: pass, 0 failures. The build wrote `Math++-0.1.0-portable.zip` and `Math++-0.1.0-x64.msi` (22.9 MB). The test installed it, checked files, shortcut, `.mpp` association and PATH, ran `mpp run`, started the IDE from the registry open command with a `.mpp` (window titled Math++, GUI subsystem, no console), then uninstalled and found everything removed. The WiX tools were copied from another worktree's `target/tools/wix3` into this one's `target/` (not committed).

## Summary of fixes

1. Import problem note no longer overlaps the import line (IDE).
2. Graph legend and readouts keep their spaces (plot, IDE).
3. One end mark on PDF proofs that end in a list (export).
4. Added `examples/long-worksheet.mpp` with its expected output and export snapshots, and the M16 test file `crates/mpp-ide/tests/m16.rs` (screenshots, problem kinds, timing).
5. Added `deny.toml`.

